# nodes.env — the SHARED environment of both node services (owner: compose-topology).
#
# WHAT BELONGS HERE: only values that must be IDENTICAL on node-a and node-b. Anything that differs
# between the two (NODE_ID, PEER_URL) is set per-service in compose.yaml, so that the ONLY difference
# between the two containers is their identity and their link — a consensus run across two nodes that
# also differ in a timeout would be measuring two different systems.
#
# WHAT MUST NEVER BE ADDED HERE: a secret, a token, a credential, a URL carrying a query-string key, or
# anything else that would be visible in `docker inspect` of BOTH containers and in `docker compose
# config`. This file is read into the container environment, and an environment variable is readable by
# anyone who can run `docker exec ... env` — security-review reads exactly that list, and the only thing
# it should be able to find is configuration. See NODE-CONTRACT §config: `describeConfig` exists to be
# served and is specified never to include a secret, which is only true if none is put here.
#
# There is nothing to keep on disk and nothing to keep between runs: every value below is a bound, not
# a record, so losing this file costs a restart and no data.

# Internal HTTP port. 8090 inside the container; the host mapping (18091/18092) is in compose.yaml and
# is deliberately NOT derivable from this value, so publishing never silently follows a port change.
PORT=8090

# Where the two PRE-CALCULATED snapshots live inside the image (baked at build time by docker-image).
# Read-only, because the rootfs is read-only: the node loads these and can never overwrite them, which
# is what makes "precalculated" a property rather than a promise.
SNAPSHOT_DIR=/app/snapshots

# Upper bound a node waits for its peer's endorsement before calling the proposal `quorum-lost`.
# A peer that answers late is NOT a peer that agreed, so this is a real deadline and not a retry budget.
COMMIT_TIMEOUT_MS=1500

# Production mode: no dev-time source maps, no reloading of the baked sources at request time.
NODE_ENV=production
